  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.6352, F1=0.6183, 7.02 GPU hrs). All three completed experiments share the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), so the impact of a learned RNA representation is completely untested. config_021 changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200 while keeping the best-performing image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), aggregation (avgpool), and fusion (weighted) fixed, making it a clean single-variable ablation. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact design axis remaining: a variational autoencoder can capture nonlinear cell-state structure that PCA (linear) cannot, potentially improving the RNA branch's contribution to the fused representation. Expected cost is moderate (~8-12 GPU hrs), comparable to config_001 since scvi_n200 adds a small VAE forward pass but the dominant cost (ViT-L image encoding + multiprofile processing) is unchanged. With 6 experiments remaining, resolving whether a learned RNA encoder helps or hurts is critical before committing further budget to downstream refinements (e.g., transformer aggregation or scgpt)."
}

